   "widgets_values": [
    "HaDeS MOSS Suite - Merge, Save and Telemetry (the sixth video tutorial)\n\nTEST RECIPE, made for the video, not a recommendation: SFT (model1) with half of Base (model2) in\nlayers 18-35. Each Block Merger slider is a group of 6 layers: 0 keeps model1, 1 takes model2.\nLayers 24-35 carry most of the SFT -> Base change (the tooltips give the measured shares).\nrecipe_override: one ratio per layer (42) plus text_embedder, time_modulation, io.\n\nMeasured on this recipe (25 steps, CFG 2.5, er_sde / simple, seed 1013):\n  - between SFT and Base: SFT's finish with some of Base's variety; the same time as SFT alone\n  - 'a woman sitting in a cafe', 16 seeds, East Asian faces: SFT 10, this recipe ~3, Base ~1-2;\n    a studio fisherman portrait: SFT 16, this recipe ~13-14, Base ~6. Name who you want in the prompt.\n\nMOSS Model Saver (muted): bfloat16 10.2 GB (stochastic rounding keeps the smallest changes; the same\nimage as the live merge), int8 ConvRot 5.4 GB (faster, small changes). The merger's info goes into\nrecipe. The file lands in output/diffusion_models: move it to models/diffusion_models to load it.\nMOSS Metadata Reader (muted): pick the saved file to read its recipe back.\nMulti-Model Merger (muted): TIES, DARE, Task Arithmetic, Model Stock or SLERP for 2-4 models;\nSLERP 0.5 gave about the same image as the Block Merger with every group at 0.5.\nTelemetry reads the merger; the PNG says Model: merge: mossImage_sft_bf16 + mossImage_base_bf16."
   ],
   "properties": {}
  }
